.TH TASKCTL 1 "September 2026" "taskctl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
taskctl \- inspect and advance repository task graphs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taskctl
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The system command runs the RPM-installed native executable. Repository-local
.B ./taskctl
uses that repository's committed toolchain lock and digest-verified cache.
Installing, upgrading or removing this RPM does not update repository pins,
initialize projects, or remove project state or caches.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR --version ", " -V ", " version
Print the tool version without repository discovery or network access.
.B version --format json
returns a machine-readable version.
.TP
.B info --format json
Inspect implementation, runtime and canonical build identity.
.TP
.B help
List supported commands and arguments.
.TP
.B init --repo PATH --id ID --toolchain LOCK
Explicitly initialize a greenfield repository. Add
.B --plan
to inspect without writing. The release's default native lock is installed at
.IR /usr/share/taskctl/toolchain.lock .
.TP
.BR doctor ", " context ", " frontier
Inspect repository validity, context and executable work. Use
.B --repo PATH
or run in the repository. An empty frontier is successful.
.TP
.BR status ", " affected " [TASK]", " history " TASK"
Inspect lifecycle separately from dependency currency and immutable task history.
Closed historical tasks keep their receipts when upstream contracts change.
.TP
.B revise TASK --file RECORD --expect-revision REVISION
Record an explicit task revision. Lifecycle cannot be changed by revision.
.TP
.B reconcile TASK --plan
Inspect the exact task HEAD and upstream observations a review must address.
.B reconcile TASK --file REVIEW --expect-revision REVISION
records an explicit review outcome, rationale and evidence. It never runs tests.
.TP
.B adopt --repo PATH --id ID --toolchain LOCK
Adopt existing code without tasking. Preserve existing source and AGENTS.md;
refuse tasking or launcher collisions. Add --plan to inspect before writing.
.PP
Mutating seed, revise, close, track and reconcile --file commands accept --plan
to report bounded writes with preimage and postimage digests. Reads are mutation-free.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
taskctl init --repo ./my-project --id example.my-project \\
  --toolchain /usr/share/taskctl/toolchain.lock
cd my-project
taskctl doctor
./taskctl frontier
.fi
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/doc/taskctl/README.rpm.md
contains packaging, offline operation and upgrade details.
.I /usr/share/doc/taskctl/docs/SEMANTIC-0.3.md
documents task records, currency, review inputs and compatibility.
.SH NOTES
Repository wrappers may download their pinned artifact on first use. This is
explicit command execution, not an RPM transaction. Private GitHub acquisition
requires a contents-read token through TASKCTL_GITHUB_TOKEN or GH_TOKEN.
TASKCTL_OFFLINE=1 requires an existing wrapper cache.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rpm (8),
.BR dnf (8)
.PP
https://github.com/brule-io/taskctl
